  "Source": "C.-W. Lin, K.-P. Chen, C.-N. Hsiao, S. Lin, and C.-K. Lee, \"Design and fabrication of an alternating dielectric multi-layer device for surface plasmon resonance sensor,\" Sens. Actuators B 113, 169-176 (2006). doi:10.1016/j.snb.2005.02.044 - Sec. 2.2 (last paragraph), Sec. 2.4 (deposition sequence), Table 1, Table 2",
  "Notes": "Conventional single-layer Au SPR chip (1 nm Cr adhesion + 50 nm Au) used as the comparison\nSpecification: Reference device (no optimisation).\nReported: Table 2 (measured, water, 632 nm, BK7 prism): SPR angle 73.9 deg (text: 'about 74 deg'), HMBW 6.5 deg (abstract FWHM 6.18), dynamic range 1.331-1.38 RIU, intensity slope 58.65 a.u./deg, intensity sensitivity 6900 a.u./RIU. Fig. 7 dashed theory: dip near 0 at ~74-75 deg, R ~90 % at ~65-70 deg (read off plot).\nNotes: Cr is deposited first on the glass, then Au, so light from the prism meets Cr first. The paper gives no Cr optical constants (database 'Cr' used); it is unclear whether the theory curve included the 1 nm Cr - remove it to test. Internal angle in BK7, p-polarisation; water from Table 1.\nLayers from Sec. 2.2 (last paragraph), Sec. 2.4 (deposition sequence), Table 1, Table 2; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours Rp minimum 0.133 % at 74.07 deg in the prism, 632 nm; paper resonance at 73.9 deg (measured), width 6.5 deg.",
